    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Payment Terms & Schedule\". Details: What are the payment amounts, milestones, and due dates?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC064-CAT017",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "Unless otherwise specified in SCC, usual payment term is 100% on receipt\nand acceptance of goods by the consignee (Stores section) and on\nproduction of all required documents by the supplier.\n22.2 For Domestic Goods: Unless otherwise specified in the SCC, payments to\nsuppliers are usually made by account payee cheque or through ECS only.\nIn case of non-payment through EFT, or where EFT facility is not available,\npayment may be released through cheque.",
