  {
    "qa_id": "IND-Q-01738",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "category_id": "CAT-014",
    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Termination for Cause\". Details: Can a party terminate this contract for cause, such as breach, default, or insolvency?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC065-CAT014",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "If the Service Provider shall dissolve or become bankrupt or insolvent or cause or suffer\nany receiver to be appointed of his business of any assets thereof compound with his\nCreditors, or being a corporation commence to be wound up, not being a member's\nvoluntary winding up for the purpose of amalgamation or reconstruction, or carry on its\nbusiness under a Receiver for the benefits of its Creditors any of them, Employer shall be\nat liberty to terminate the Contract forthwith upon coming to know of the happening of\nany such event as aforesaid by notice in writing to the Service Provider or to give the\nReceiver or Liquidator or other person, the option of carrying out the Contract subject to\nhis providing a guarantee up to an amount to be agreed upon by the Employer for due and\nfaithful performance of the Contract.",
        "answer_start": 40232,
        "answer_end": 41057,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0154"
      },
      {
        "text": "If the Bidder/Service Provider is found to have indulged in Corrupt/ Fraudulent\n/Collusive/Coercive practices, the Contract shall be terminated and the Bidder/ Service\nProvider shall be banned for future business with BCPL. The detailed procedure for\nbanning including suspension is elaborated in the tender document.",
        "answer_start": 41168,
        "answer_end": 41485,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0156"
      }
    ],
    "is_impossible": false,
    "gold_paragraph_ids": [
      "PAR-DOC065-0154",
      "PAR-DOC065-0156"
    ],
    "doc_origin": "collected_real",
