    "question": "when do i get paid and how much",
    "question_register": "naive_layperson",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC065-CAT017",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "The price to be paid by the Employer to Service Provider for the whole of the Service to\nbe done and for the performance of all the obligations undertaken by the Service Provider\nunder the Contract Documents shall be ascertained by the application of the respective\nSchedule of Rates (the inclusive nature of which is more particularly defined by way of\napplication but not of limitation, with the succeeding sub-clause of this clause) and\npayment to be made accordingly for the Services actually executed and approved by the\nEngineer-in-Charge. The sum so ascertained shall (except only as and to the extent\nexpressly provided herein) constitute the sole and inclusive remuneration of the Service\nProvider under the Contract and no further or other payment whatsoever shall be or\nbecome due or payable to the Service Provider under the Contract.",
        "answer_start": 74525,
        "answer_end": 75371,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0259"
      }
    ],
    "is_impossible": false,
    "gold_paragraph_ids": [
      "PAR-DOC065-0259"
    ],
    "doc_origin": "collected_real",
    "tier": "A",
    "split": "core",
    "annotator_ids": [
      "Pushkar SHarma, lead of project"
    ],
    "annotation_pass": "P1-model-assisted",
    "model_assisted": true,
    "adjudicated": false,
    "jaccard_agreement": null,
    "annotator_notes": ""
  },
  {
    "qa_id": "IND-Q-01750",
    "doc_id": "DOC-065",
    "category_id": "CAT-019",
    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Cap on Liability\". Details: Is there a cap on liability or a time limit for bringing claims under this contract?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC065-CAT019",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "Notwithstanding anything contrary contained herein, the aggregate total liability of\nService Provider to Employer under the Contract shall not exceed the Total Contract\nValue, except that this clause shall not limit the liability of the Service Provider for\nfollowing:\n(a) In the event of breach of any Applicable Law;\n(b) In the event of fraud, willful misconduct or illegal or unlawful acts, or gross\nNegligence of the Service Provider or any person acting on behalf of the Service\nProvider; or\n(c) In the event of acts or omissions of the Service Provider which are contrary to the\nmost elementary rules of diligence which a conscientious Service Provider would have\nfollowed in similar circumstances; or\n(d) In the event of any claim or loss or damage arising out of infringement of Intellectual\nProperty; or\n(e) For any damage to any third party, including death or injury of any third party caused\nby the Service Provider or any person or firm acting on behalf of the Service Provider in\nexecuting the Works/Services.",
        "answer_start": 71205,
        "answer_end": 72228,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC065-0251"
      }
    ],
    "is_impossible": false,
    "gold_paragraph_ids": [
