  {
    "qa_id": "IND-Q-01903",
    "doc_id": "DOC-068",
    "category_id": "CAT-022",
    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Warranty Duration\". Details: What is the duration of any warranty against defects or errors in goods or services provided?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC068-CAT022",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "within a period twelve (12) months from the date if issue of completion\ncertificate by OWNER/CONSULTANT it shall be rectified or replaced by\nCONTRACTOR at his own expense as deemed necessary by the Engineer-in-\nCharge. If CONTRACTOR fails to do so within reasonable period or if in the\nopinion of OWNER/CONSULTANT, CONTRACTOR is unable to do so, or the\nrepair / replacement cannot wait till CONTRACTOR is able to do it,\nOWNER/CONSULTANT may either directly or through such other agencies as\nOWNER/CONSULTANT may deem fit, get defective part of WORK made good,\nall at the risk and cost of CONTRACTOR. Notwithstanding the period specified\nabove, in case of civil constructions, the period of warranty will extend at least up\nto the end of first monsoon after the WORK is taken over",
        "answer_start": 61390,
        "answer_end": 62169,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0171"
      },
      {
        "text": "An item of WORK so repaired or replaced shall carry a further warranty as per\nArticle-30.2 above.",
        "answer_start": 62192,
        "answer_end": 62289,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC068-0172"
      }
    ],
    "is_impossible": false,
    "gold_paragraph_ids": [
      "PAR-DOC068-0171",
      "PAR-DOC068-0172"
    ],
