    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "category_id": "CAT-013",
    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Termination for Convenience\". Details: Can a party terminate this contract for convenience, without cause?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC069-CAT013",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "If at any time after acceptance of the tender, Engineer-in-Charge shall decide to abandonor reduce\nthe scope of the works for any reason whatsoever and hence not require thewhole or any part of the\nworks to be carried out, the Engineer-in-Charge shall give notice inwriting to that effect to the\ncontractor and the contractor shall act accordingly in the matter.The contractor shall have no claim\nto any payment of compensation or otherwisewhatsoever, on account of any profit or advantage\nwhich he might have derived from theexecution of the works in full but which he did not derive in\nconsequence of the foreclosureof the whole or part of the works.",
        "answer_start": 73000,
