  {
    "qa_id": "IND-Q-01978",
    "doc_id": "DOC-069",
    "category_id": "CAT-023",
    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Delivery & Milestone Obligations\". Details: What are the delivery dates, milestones, or completion schedules?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC069-CAT023",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "As soon as possible after the Contract is concluded, the Contractor shall submit aTime and\nProgress Chart for each mile stone and get it approved by the Department. The Chart shall be\nprepared in direct relation to the time stated in theContract documents for completion of items of the\nworks. It shall indicate theforecast of the dates of commencement and completion of various trades\nofsections of the work and may be amended as necessary by agreement between theEngineer-in-\nCharge and the Contractor within the limitations of time imposed inthe Contract documents, and\nfurther to ensure good progress during the execution of the work, the contractor shall in all cases in\nwhich the time allowed for any work,exceeds one month (save for special jobs for which a separate\nprogramme hasbeen agreed upon) complete the work as per mile stones given in Schedule ‘ F’.",
        "answer_start": 19147,
        "answer_end": 20012,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC069-0049"
      }
    ],
    "is_impossible": false,
    "gold_paragraph_ids": [
