    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Termination for Cause\". Details: Can a party terminate this contract for cause, such as breach, default, or insolvency?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC083-CAT014",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "In the event that Licensee defaults in the payment in full of any amount\nrequired to be paid under this Agreement on the date such payment is due, in\naddition to utilizing any other legal and/or equitable remedies, IITK shall have the\nright by written notice to Licensee within ____ days after such default either (i) to\nterminate the exclusivity, if any, of the license hereunder in (by amending the word\n\"exclusive\" in the License Grant to read \"non-exclusive\") without any reduction in\nany of the payments due from Licensee or (ii) to terminate this Agreement.",
        "answer_start": 17163,
        "answer_end": 17726,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0059"
      },
      {
        "text": "In the event that either party to this Agreement defaults in the performance of\nany of its obligations hereunder (other than the default referred to in Section 10.1.\n(Termination), hereof) and fails to cure such default within ____ days after written\nnotice of such default from such other party, the other party shall have the right by\nwritten notice to the defaulting party within ____ days after the expiration of such\n_____ day period to terminate this Agreement.",
        "answer_start": 17734,
        "answer_end": 18201,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC083-0060"
      }
