    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "As part of the empanelment process, MeitY has mandated CSPs to have following\ncertifications.\na. ISO 27001:2013 – Information security management systems requirements\n(Data Center and the Cloud Services should be certified for the ISO 27001\nstandard)\nb. ISO 20000:1 - Service management system requirements (NOC and SOC offered\nfor the Data Center and the managed services quality should be certified for\nISO 20000:1)\nc. ISO 27017 - Code of practice for information security controls based on ISO/IEC\n27002 for Cloud Services\nd. ISO 27018 - Code of practice for protection of Personally Identifiable\nInformation (PII) in Public Clouds acting as PII processors",
        "answer_start": 74651,
        "answer_end": 75310,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0130"
      }
    ],
    "is_impossible": false,
    "gold_paragraph_ids": [
      "PAR-DOC085-0130"
    ],
    "doc_origin": "collected_real",
    "tier": "A",
    "split": "core",
    "annotator_ids": [
      "Pushkar SHarma, lead of project"
    ],
    "annotation_pass": "P1-model-assisted",
    "model_assisted": true,
    "adjudicated": false,
    "jaccard_agreement": null,
    "annotator_notes": ""
  },
  {
    "qa_id": "IND-Q-02788",
    "doc_id": "DOC-085",
    "category_id": "CAT-026",
    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Personal Data Handling\". Details: How is personal data collected, stored, processed, or transferred under this contract?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC085-CAT026",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "The Managed Service Provider shall implement reasonable and appropriate measures\nto secure the Purchaser’s data and content against accidental or unlawful loss, access\nor disclosure.\n(ii)\nIf the data is classified as sensitive / confidential / restricted, the Managed Service\nProvider shall ensure that the data is encrypted as part of a standard security process\nfor sensitive / confidential / restricted content or choose the right cryptographic\nalgorithms evaluating security, performance, and compliance requirements specific to\nthe Purchaser’s application and may choose from multiple key management options\napproved by the Purchaser.\n(iii)\nThe Managed Service Provider shall notify the Purchaser promptly in the event of\nsecurity incidents or intrusions, or requests from foreign governments / their agencies\nfor access to the data, to enable the Purchaser to manage these events proactively.\n(iv)\nThe Managed Service Provider shall not delete any data at the end of the\nAgreement/Contract (for a maximum of 45 days beyond the expiry of the Agreement)\nwithout the express approval of the Purchaser. After the approval to delete the data is\naccorded by the Purchaser, the Managed Service Provider shall ensure that all the\nstorage blocks or multiple copies of data, if any, are unallocated or zeroed out so that\nit cannot be recovered. If due to some regulatory reasons, it is required to securely\ndecommission data, the Purchaser can implement data encryption at rest using\nPurchaser’s managed keys, which are not stored in the Cloud. Then Purchaser may\ndelete the key used to protect the decommissioned data, making it irrecoverable.",
        "answer_start": 77640,
        "answer_end": 79280,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0134"
      },
      {
        "text": "The Managed Service Provider shall store all types of data (including but not limited to\naccount & user access data, text, audio, video, image, software, machine image, and\nany computational results that the Purchaser or any end user derives through their use\nof the Managed Service Provider’s services) within the Indian Territory and as per the\nterms and conditions specified in the CSP’s Empanelment RFP; and shall not take out /\nallow to take out any kind of data outside of India unless it is explicitly approved by\nthe Purchaser.",
        "answer_start": 84266,
        "answer_end": 84801,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC085-0142"
      }
    ],
    "is_impossible": false,
    "gold_paragraph_ids": [
      "PAR-DOC085-0134",
      "PAR-DOC085-0142"
    ],
    "doc_origin": "collected_real",
