  {
    "qa_id": "IND-Q-02827",
    "doc_id": "DOC-086",
    "category_id": "CAT-014",
    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Termination for Cause\". Details: Can a party terminate this contract for cause, such as breach, default, or insolvency?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC086-CAT014",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "In the event that (i) the Concessionaire does not procure fulfilment of any or all of the\nConditions Precedent set forth in Clause 4.1.3 within a period of 180 (one hundred and eighty)\ndays from the date of this Agreement, and (ii) the delay has not occurred as a result of failure\nto fulfil the obligations under Clause 4.1.2 or other breach of this Agreement by the Authority,\nor due to Force Majeure, the Concessionaire shall pay to the Authority, Damages in an amount\ncalculated at the rate of 0.2% (zero point two per cent) of the Performance Security for each\nday’s delay until the fulfilment of such Conditions Precedent, subject to a maximum of 100%\n(hundred percent) of the Performance Security.",
        "answer_start": 65261,
