  {
    "qa_id": "IND-Q-02902",
    "doc_id": "DOC-087",
    "category_id": "CAT-014",
    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Termination for Cause\". Details: Can a party terminate this contract for cause, such as breach, default, or insolvency?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC087-CAT014",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "The other party is in material breach of its obligations under this Agreement and / or, in the\ncase of such breaches capable of being remedied, fails to remedy that breach within thirty\ndays of receiving notice of such breach; or",
        "answer_start": 52374,
        "answer_end": 52603,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC087-0195"
      },
      {
        "text": "In case of breach of Contract or in the event  of not fulfilling the minimum\nrequirements / statutory requirements, the Client shall have the  right to terminate the contract\nforthwith in addition to forfeiting the performance security amount deposited by the\ncontractor and initiating administrative actions for blacklisting etc.  solely at the discretion of\nthe Competent authority of the office of the Client.",
        "answer_start": 45666,
