    "doc_id": "DOC-097",
    "category_id": "CAT-014",
    "question": "Highlight the parts (if any) of this contract related to \"Termination for Cause\". Details: Can a party terminate this contract for cause, such as breach, default, or insolvency?",
    "question_register": "canonical",
    "intent_group_id": "IG-DOC097-CAT014",
    "answers": [
      {
        "text": "If the manager at any time willfully neglects or refuses or from illness or other cause becomes or is unable to perform any of the duties under this agreement, the employer may suspend his salary (and sum by way of percentage) during such neglect, negligence or inability as aforesaid and may further immediately terminate the engagement of the manager without giving any such notice or making such payment or salary in advance as hereinbefore provided.",
        "answer_start": 5133,
        "answer_end": 5586,
        "paragraph_id": "PAR-DOC097-0014"
      },
      {
        "text": "The manager will at his own expense find and provide two respectable sureties to the amount of Rs............... each for his good conduct and for the due performance by him of this engagement and if he fails to do so for a period of three months from this date, the employer may terminate his services forthwith.",
        "answer_start": 5592,
        "answer_end": 5905,
